cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: >-
  If you use this software, benchmark protocol, or empirical cross-section
  geometry artifacts, please cite both the software release and the companion
  manuscript as below.
title: >-
  ann-xs-estimation: Hard Manning + Continuity Hybrid Versus Unconstrained
  Machine Learning for Reach-Scale River Cross-Section Geometry Across the
  Continental United States
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-16"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
license: "BSD-3-Clause"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ahmetnazim/ann-xs-estimation"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX"
abstract: >-
  Reproducible Scientific Software Development Life Cycle (S-SDLC) research
  codebase evaluating whether a hard Manning + continuity physics-informed
  neural hybrid (M5, combining an I_blind roughness head with a differentiable
  Picard-solved Manning + Dingman projection layer Phi using 513-node
  tanh-sinh wet-perimeter quadrature, quad_level = 6, quad_trunc = 4.0,
  tau_l = 1e-10) improves reach-scale river cross-section geometry estimation
  over unconstrained machine learning and empirical baselines across the
  conterminous United States (CONUS). Implements the full model ladder
  (M-null, M0, M1, M2-MLP, M2-XGB, M3, M4, M5, M6-NN, M6-XGB, and A_J Jobson
  baseline) with deep-ensemble Gaussian-mixture uncertainty quantification,
  evaluated across n = 3,988 ungauged HYDROSWOT sites (8 Fenneman & Johnson
  physiographic divisions; n = 9,673 post-QC S-RND records) and 131 independent
  USACE eHydro survey locations across 18 rivers (S-IND), under a
  cryptographically hash-chained three-event scoring ledger.
